[N 33-33 Back on Track]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\Shaman only, picked by hand: for a shaman who ran Gnomeregan, the City of Dalaran and Razorfen Kraul ahead of the route and never played chapters 27 and 29. Veyric's totem quest, the Scarlet Monastery pickup at the Dalaran crater, Aerie Peak for Expert Leatherworking and its flight point, the Ironforge lead-ins, then Stormwind for chapter 30.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel check|r  -  this chapter wants level 33, the level chapter 30 (Stranglethorn Vale) wants. Nothing in it needs more than level 30 and nothing in it is a fight. Still 32 at the end: go on anyway, chapter 30's own level check says what to kill first
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffffffBack on track at 33|r  -  you stand at Veyric Thunderhame in Arathi with Elemental Aid just handed in (the end of the Razorfen Kraul dungeon chapter); hearth = Stormwind and it stays there. This chapter takes from chapters 27 and 29 only what a later chapter needs: Storm, Earth, and Fire, the two Scarlet Monastery Library quests, the lead-ins for Desolace and the Badlands, the Aerie Peak flight point and Expert Leatherworking. 12,010 quest XP is picked up for later chapters and none is handed in. Everything else in those two chapters is left behind

[A Shaman] At [TAR259023 Veyric Thunderhame], [QA79358 Storm, Earth, and Fire] (shaman only, requires level 30: he gives you The Walks of Shaman. 5 each of the Twisted Fire, Earth, Air and Water Totems from the Stonevault (Badlands), the Lost Ones (Swamp of Sorrows), the Maraudine (Desolace) and the Mirefin (Dustwallow) - collected in chapters 32, 33, 35 and 37 and handed in here in chapter 39 for 3,600 XP) [G59.8,27.6 Arathi Highlands]
[OC][A Shaman] Heed My Call (96135) and The Tempest's Weapons (96016) stay in Veyric's list for the level-40 block (chapters 39 and 39c)
[OC]Back to Refuge Pointe the way you came, about 24 map units south-west
At [TAR2835 Cedrik Prose], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Southshore]|r (direct) [G45.7,46.1 Arathi Highlands]

[OC]|cffffffffTo the crater|r  -  on foot from Southshore, Dalaran has no flight point. Keep WEST of the road north: Tarren Mill in the north-east is a Horde town. Cross the Hillsbrad Fields, then take the pass in the north-west corner into Alterac and down into the crater
Leave Southshore north-west to the Hillsbrad Fields [G33,42 Hillsbrad Foothills]
Go on north-west through the pass into the Alterac Mountains [G18,72 Alterac Mountains]
At [TAR264265 Magus Olvek], [QA96800 Past Due] (2,850 XP + 45s, requires level 30: The Lost Magic of the Runemasters from the Scarlet Monastery Library - carried to chapter 34, handed in to Olvek on a later crater visit) [G9.8,63.4 Alterac Mountains]
[OC]Starving Arcane (92457) is still in your log: the Image of Archmage Modera, who takes it, stands about 150 yards east of Olvek - for the day you run the City of Dalaran again

[OC]|cffffffffAerie Peak|r  -  the Wildhammer town in the Hinterlands has a shaman trainer and the Expert Leatherworking trainer, and its flight point is new to you, so the first trip is on foot. The road is the Classic one, |cffffcc00unverified|r on Forever. Do not take the road north out of Arathi: it runs past Hammerfall's level 50 guards
Back through the pass and south-east across the Hillsbrad Fields to Southshore; stay south of Tarren Mill, the Horde town in the north [G49.3,52.3 Hillsbrad Foothills]
Walk north-east out of Southshore across the Hillsbrad Fields and through the eastern hills past Durnholde Keep (Syndicate 20-22, Elder Gray Bears and Giant Moss Creepers 24-26: grey or green to you) to the Wildhammer post of Granistad and Kurdros (friendly), at the foot of the pass into the Hinterlands [G84.2,32.8 Hillsbrad Foothills]
[OC]Up the pass and west to the Aerie Peak gate. Mangy Silvermanes (41-42) and Old Cliff Jumper (42 rare) roam east and south of the gate: come in from the west and do not wander south-east. The Wildhammer Sentries and the Trained Razorbeaks are friendly
At flight master [TAR8018 Guthrum Thunderfist], get the [P Aerie Peak] flight point [G11.1,46.2 The Hinterlands]
At [TAR11097 Drakk Stonehand], [T] train Expert Leatherworking (50s): your Leatherworking is capped at 150 until you do. His character-level gate is |cffffcc00unverified|r [G13.4,43.5 The Hinterlands]
[OC][A Shaman] Farseer Maret Firetend trains shamans in Aerie Peak (the Wowhead list says like Eldrun, |cffffcc00unverified|r in game): nothing to buy at 33, the level 34 ranks wait for a later trainer stop
At [TAR8018 Guthrum Thunderfist], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Ironforge]|r (direct, about 4 minutes) [G11.1,46.2 The Hinterlands]

